  "design": {
    "enemySide": "north",
    "tacticalIdentity": "Interlocking urban loops replace the exposed central firing lane. A temple court, a residential block on the bent avenue and the Colosseum shell split the middle into short fights with cross streets and two-sided exits. Patrols cross between the Forum and the avenue instead of following parallel perimeter lanes. The second group brings the single howitzer; four supply pockets reward moving north and across flanks.",
    "reference": {
      "place": "Roman Forum, Colosseum and Arch of Constantine, Rome, Italy",
      "kind": "real",
      "kept": [
        "Colosseum ellipse east of the Forum with a partly missing southern outer facade",
        "Via dei Fori Imperiali linking the northern city approach to the Colosseum square",
        "Arch of Constantine south of the amphitheatre with three passages",
        "Forum temple columns and excavated masonry courts",
        "Palatine-side gardens and pine groves west and south of the ruins"
      ],
      "simplified": [
        "Generic urban buildings represent the surrounding residential blocks",
        "Standard forest canopy suggests Roman pine groves",
        "Colosseum arcade count is reduced; two axial gates are widened for tanks",
        "Forum columns evoke the Temple of Castor and Pollux without reconstructing the entire temple",
        "Pantheon, Vittoriano and underground archaeological structures are omitted",
        "The allied field workshop and barricades are fictional battle positions",
        "The avenue bends around a compressed residential block; temple courts and transverse paths create playable loops rather than a literal street survey"
      ]
    },
